{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486141-primordial-forest-spirits","id":1486141,"title":"Primordial Forest Spirits?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-10T00:50:32-07:00","id":1486141,"title":"Primordial Forest Spirits?","content":"I am working on a setting in the pacific northwestern united states' temperate rainforests (google oregon rainforest), and wanted to hear what y'all's recommendations are for spirits that can represent prehistoric forests. I at first assumed it could be some kind of fungus, though the only references I can find to fungus spirits is a bane. I am imagining a spirit at some primordial abscessed forgotten caern that is needing to be appeased. Trees in the region include doug firs and alders, as well as white oak. Common animals are ravens, elk, wolves, spotted owls, pine martens, and black bears. In many of the forests here, they have no 'floor', it's just trees piled on trees over centuries of growth and decay. Could something like a Nameless apply here? Something mossy and covered in ferns?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":27167,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","user":"mundusartis","date":". 07-10-2022, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T02:49:09-07:00","id":1486143,"title":"","content":"Go with the fungus if you feel it! It's a cool idea, and my guess is the only reason they made fungus spirits banes in the books is because fungi are commonly associated with decay- meaning they were on clean-up duty before the Wyrm went mad, and then got corrupted. However, the decay association applies mostly for molds only, not all fungi. Having the stereotypical expectation of fungus = evil subverted would be a good opportunity to surprise the players.<br /> <br /> There are many cool attributes of fungi you can use to outline the spirit's characteristics:<ul><li>Many species have a symbiotic relationship with other things. Lichens are actually a composite organism of fungus, alga, and/or bacteria. Mushrooms exchange nutrients with trees. This could be represented by the spirit displaying a weird duality of aspects and powers.</li> <li>Mushroom hyphae can grow huge and deep. Oregon famously hosts a species that covers four square miles with a single specimen (<i>Armillaria ostoyae</i>). The spirit could have great awareness and agency over its domain. Maybe the caern is located within the decaying forest floor, with the hyphae of the fungus forming a cave.</li> <li>Slime molds are mobile fungi with often alien life-cycles. There is a species I know of (<i>Dictyostelium</i>) that can form a composite body out of individual specimens. An associated power could be for the spirit to be able to disperse into many individuals or aggregate into a single form at will.</li> </ul><br /> Don't let RAW stand in the way of a good idea, especially for things like this. Just take the stats of a spirit with an appropriate power level and look up or invent some Charms that go with the theme and what your narrative needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T04:32:14-07:00","id":1486144,"title":"","content":"A spirit of the idea that discarded material is lying around everywhere, witnessing everything in a surprisingly huge radius, gathering wisdom from a perspective from the bottom up... I would shamelessly take a look on the rules of the Totem &quot;All-knowing Trash Heap&quot; and tweak it to make sense for a forest, never telling my players that we're using a relabeled trash spirit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Ban of having to choose a region of the Heap and having to serve and protect it could be used as is.<br /> The boon of answering a question each moon cycle seems to be an awesome fit as well for that primordial forest-floor-witnessing everything.<br /> The Spirit granting points in Enigmas is a fit too, maybe the 'investigation' would have to be changed into survival, depending on whether your table uses investigation for rolls to notice things in the woods too or not.<br /> The boon of having the Garou freely communicate with each other as long as they carry a piece of the Heap could be played just as is or it could be changed into 'as long as they touch the same forest ground' instead of carrying a decaying piece of tree. Depends on the playstyle at your table.<br /> <br /> A honorable mention would go to the gift Dumpster Diving, which isn't a direct trait of the Trashheap Totem but local teleportation trough delving into the ground and reemerging in another part of the forest might be worth consideration as one of the potential powers this Forest Floor Totem could grant if it's the Caern Totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27469-ilsaena","name":"Ilsaena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T06:05:34-07:00","id":1486147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ilsaena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486141-primordial-forest-spirits?p=1486144#post1486144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A spirit of the idea that discarded material is lying around everywhere, witnessing everything in a surprisingly huge radius, gathering wisdom from a perspective from the bottom up... I would shamelessly take a look on the rules of the Totem &quot;All-knowing Trash Heap&quot; and tweak it to make sense for a forest, never telling my players that we're using a relabeled trash spirit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's a nice fit for a reskin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ilsaena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486141-primordial-forest-spirits?p=1486144#post1486144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The boon of having the Garou freely communicate with each other as long as they carry a piece of the Heap could be played just as is or it could be changed into 'as long as they touch the same forest ground' instead of carrying a decaying piece of tree. Depends on the playstyle at your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a type of tree mushroom called <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auricularia_auricula-judae\" target=\"_blank\">Wood Ear</a> or Jelly Ear that would make a good replacement focus item.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com